  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "foundations-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 620,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "The system itself, drawn so it can be checked rather than described.\n\nEvery value on these boards is the one the screens use. Where a screen and a foundation disagree, the foundation is the defect report.\n\nThe rule underneath all of it: colour is reinforcement, never signal. Every state is carried by shape, fill, size or position first — the greyscale strip is the proof."
    },
    {
      "id": "setup-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 520,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "Seven steps, each with a verify state. No step advances on assumption. The route mismatch is the one halt — there is no continue-anyway."
    },
    {
      "id": "integrated",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 400,
      "page": "page-3",
      "text": "Integrated: Editorial's typography and rhythm as the base, Timeline's activity chart on the home, Instrument's density in the Log, and the drill-in kept as it was.\n\nThe drawer replaces the tab bar. The drawer footer carries the storage budget (D26), because on this product that is a thing you actually watch."
    },
    {
      "id": "detail-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 520,
      "page": "page-5",
      "text": "Four states, one screen each, and the same inspection surface under all of them. Correction is three tiers; the propagation screen is the point of the whole flow."
    },
    {
      "id": "failures-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -170,
      "w": 620,
      "page": "page-9",
      "text": "Every row of functional spec §12, drawn as the screen the operator would be looking at when it happens. Each shows the response column, not just the failure. Amber is degradation; red is only for capture actually stopping."
    },
    {
      "id": "explorations",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 360,
      "page": "page-11",
      "text": "The two original direction sketches, kept for reference. The Instrument direction is not here separately — it became the Log view."
    }
  ],
